white|colour|ADJECTIVE|having the lightest ordinary colour|Having the colour of fresh snow or plain milk.|màu trắng|A white curtain covered the narrow window.|Một tấm rèm trắng che ô cửa sổ hẹp.|Before a noun or after a linking verb; this proposed sense is colour, not a category of people.|0
white|colour-noun|NOUN|the colour white|The light colour seen in fresh snow or plain milk.|màu trắng|She chose white for the walls and blue for the doors.|Cô ấy chọn màu trắng cho tường và màu xanh dương cho cửa.|Usually uncountable for the colour; this record does not propose a racial or other unrelated noun sense.|1
actual|real|ADJECTIVE|real rather than supposed|Real or existing in fact, rather than imagined, expected, or merely claimed.|thực tế; thật sự|The actual cost was lower than the estimate.|Chi phí thực tế thấp hơn mức ước tính.|Usually before a noun; actual means real, not necessarily current.|0
hopeful|feeling-hope|ADJECTIVE|expecting a desired outcome|Feeling that a desired outcome may happen.|hy vọng; lạc quan|The applicants are hopeful that more places will become available.|Những người nộp đơn hy vọng sẽ có thêm chỗ.|Hopeful that takes a clause; hopeful about names the outcome. Hope is not certainty.|0
hopeful|promising|ADJECTIVE|giving reason for hope|Giving people a reason to expect a good result.|đầy triển vọng; đem lại hy vọng|The first trial produced hopeful signs of progress.|Lần thử đầu tiên cho thấy những dấu hiệu tiến triển đầy triển vọng.|Can describe signs or developments rather than a person feeling hope; does not guarantee success.|1
mental|mind-related|ADJECTIVE|relating to the mind|Relating to the mind, thinking, or emotions rather than primarily to the body.|thuộc tinh thần; thuộc trí óc|Solving the puzzle required considerable mental effort.|Giải câu đố đòi hỏi nhiều nỗ lực trí óc.|Usually before a noun such as effort or health; mental effort does not by itself mean a mental illness.|0
responsibility|duty|NOUN|duty to take care of something|A duty to deal with something or take care of a person or task.|trách nhiệm|Checking the equipment is the supervisor's responsibility.|Kiểm tra thiết bị là trách nhiệm của người giám sát.|Responsibility for names the duty or person cared for; responsibilities can list individual duties.|0
responsibility|accountability|NOUN|being answerable for an outcome|The state of being answerable for an action or its consequences.|trách nhiệm về hành động hoặc hậu quả|She accepted responsibility for sending the wrong document.|Cô ấy nhận trách nhiệm về việc gửi nhầm tài liệu.|Accept or take responsibility for plus a noun or ing form; distinct from an assigned task before it is done.|-
